    "The current async-load candidate does not show a large hot resident lookup loss. Versus original, independent throughput is +0.03%; dependent is -0.60% with cycles/op +0.42%. This does not resolve the separate fixed-work insertion regression.",
    "Masking benefits original and main. Mask-original/original is +5.43% throughput and -6.64% cycles/op for independent access; +1.36% throughput and -1.27% cycles/op for dependent access. Independent throughput confidence interval includes zero, but its cycle interval and all three throughput block means favor masking.",
    "Original, async-load and mask-original each retire four more instructions/op than main; mask-main retires two fewer than main. Mask-original cycle improvement occurs with unchanged retired instruction count, consistent with reduced instruction cost/dependencies or layout rather than fewer instructions. These counters do not measure micro-op count or isolate divider latency.",
    "Dependent main controls show a substantial first-block slowdown, widening all candidate/main intervals. Do not use those intervals as evidence for a precise sub-three-percent bound.",
